  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="ES">Output 2.2. Increased capacity of the member States to apply international labour standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="ES">CEACR Observation on C111/Peru:

&#x201c;With reference to its request to evaluate the consequences of the differences of legislative treatment and of indirect discrimination in the special labour regimes (in agriculture, domestic work and micro-enterprises), the Committee notes with satisfaction that the agricultural sector is now governed by Act No. 31110 on the agrarian labour regime and incentives for the agrarian sector and irrigation, agricultural exports and agro-industry (published on 31 December 2021) and its Regulations, and that section 6 of the Act prohibits discrimination and acts of violence or harassment and establishes protection measures for pregnant and nursing workers.&#x201d;
 The Office provided a Technical Memo on the Regulations to the Ministry of Labour and Promotion of Employment on 13 January 2021. The Memo was also shared with organizations of workers and employers in Peru.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="ES">2.2.1. Number of cases of progress in the application of ratified Conventions noted with satisfaction by the supervisory bodies</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="ES">Output 2.1. Increased capacity of the member States to ratify international labour standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="ES">El d&#xed;a 18 de junio de 2021, Per&#xfa; ratific&#xf3; el Protocolo de 2014 relativo al Convenio sobre el Trabajo Forzoso, 1920 (n&#xfa;m. 29). Con el apoyo del gobierno de Estados Unidos, la OIT desarroll&#xf3; una sesi&#xf3;n informativa sobre la importancia de la ratificaci&#xf3;n del P29 en colaboraci&#xf3;n con el Ministerio de Justicia y Derechos Humanos el 25 de agosto de 2020, as&#xed; como una sesi&#xf3;n t&#xe9;cnica dirigida a la Comisi&#xf3;n Nacional para la Lucha contra el Trabajo Forzoso el 02 en febrero de 2021.  Como resultado de ello, se prioriz&#xf3; el proceso de ratificaci&#xf3;n del P29 en la agenda gobierno. En marzo 2021 la OIT apoy&#xf3; el desarrollo de materiales informativos para promover la ratificaci&#xf3;n del P29 en alianza con la Federaci&#xf3;n Nacional de Trabajadoras del Hogar. Por &#xfa;ltimo, en marzo de 2021 la OIT sostuvo una reuni&#xf3;n con la Presidenta del Congreso de la Rep&#xfa;blica, lo que trajo como resultado que se incluya el expediente del proyecto de norma para ratificar el P29 en la agenda de la sesi&#xf3;n de pleno, dando lugar a su ratificaci&#xf3;n.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="ES">2.1.1. Number of ratifications of fundamental and governance Conventions or Protocols</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
